    "session_id": "3ff3617f-60c9-4263-8e8d-ec0b31c0f0b4",
    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. There's a single runnable test class (`AcceptanceTest`; the other two files under `src/test` are the non-executable `AcceptanceBase` harness and a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag on owner creation, mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` feature end-to-end.\n\n**Behavior:** When an owner is created and their city already holds **40\u201349** owners, the created owner's `capacityWarning` is `true`; otherwise `false`. The hard `409` rejection at 50 is unchanged (since a create past that rejection always has `< 50` owners in the city, `>= 40` cleanly captures the 40\u201349 band).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean schema field to the `Owner` model (this is what generates the `OwnerDto` field at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `capacity_warning` column field plus getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` column next to `bulk_signup_warning`.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant.\n   - Split the old `rejectCityAtCapacity(city)` into `countOwnersInCity(city)` (counts once) + `rejectCityAtCapacity(city, ownersInCity)` \u2014 mirroring the existing `countRegisteredOn` / `rejectDailyRegistrationLimitReached` pattern, avoiding a second stream over all owners.\n   - In `addOwner`, set `owner.setCapacityWarning(ownersInCity >= CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD)`.\n\nMapStruct maps the field automatically by name (no explicit `@Mapping` needed, same as `bulkSignupWarning`).",
